-- title:
--   Nonzero two- and three-torsion parameters give exceptional supports
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. Write $H=G[2]=\{u:2u=0\}$, $K=G[3]=\{v:3v=0\}$, $h=|H|$, $t=|K|$, $n=|G|$, and $q=|2G|$. For a triple support $S$, let $\mathcal F(S)$ be all three-element supports having the same ordered pair-sum counts, and $\mathcal O(S)=\{S+u:u\in H\}$. An ordinary fibre has size $h$; an exceptional fibre has size $2h$. For any fibre $F$, put $F^\circ=\{S\in F:0\notin S\}$. Put $P(a,d,v)=\{a,a+v,a+v+d\}$. For $a\in G$, $d\in H\setminus\{0\}$ and $v\in K\setminus\{0\}$,
--
--   $$P(a,d,v)\text{ is exceptional}.$$
--
--   This describes the finite triple-support square fibres.
-- source:
